--- v2/routines/inbox.md
+++ v3/routines/inbox.md
@@ -1 +1 @@
-RUN RECORD (AR-20261018-8). Before your first Notion write, fix this run's id once: Bash printenv CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID (the provider's id for this run); if empty, run once echo "syn-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)-$(od -An -N4 -tx1 /dev/urandom | tr -d ' \n')" and label it synthetic. Keep it for the whole run; never derive it again. Then one Activity: Kind Note, Source empty, Summary "Run inbox <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM> JST: Started", Source ID "run:inbox:<run id>", Date = the start, Captured today, no People, Engagement, Deal or Episode. If the create response is unclear, query that Source ID before writing again: reuse a row that has it, never a second. Another run never shares your id, even in the same minute. Your last write: update that row's Summary to "Run inbox <start> JST: <Completed|No-op|Partial|Failed>" (No-op: nothing to act on; Partial: a step failed or was skipped; Failed: stopped early) and its page body to the report, plus the end time, deployment reference (Unknown unless known), counts, errors, blocked items with their next owner and links to the Activities this run logged. Never invent a version, cost, id or delivery. The run id never replaces a send's idempotency key or any business dedupe. A run record is not stakeholder activity: it never sets Last activity, Waiting on or a contact date, never links to a row and never counts toward the send cap. If writing it fails, retry once, then carry on and say so in the report; never repeat a business action because of it.
